##
    A project that says something a project cannot say.

    The whole vocabulary is 'project', 'source', 'reference', 'entry', 'output', 'ignore',
    'end project', and the language's two comment forms. A project file describes a build, not a
    computation, so it borrows nothing else from the language — and a word that is none of those
    is a mistake rather than something to read hopefully.

    Both lines are reported rather than only the first. A file written from memory of some other
    build system holds several of these, and hearing about one per run would mean building once
    for each word.
##

project Unknown
    include ../runtime/overflow.pc
    exclude ../runtime/divide-by-zero.pc
end project
